  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1e7e6f61-82ba-4df6-8ae1-65ffc479b6cd-image.png\" style=\"width: 230px; height: 190px;\" /><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br />Since, for equilateral triangle centroid in center and circumcenter is the same therefore length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><msqrt><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><br />As centroid divide median in the ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><br />Centre of the circle would be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;&#160;</mo></math> Answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>",
